  ($hk$ايش أخبارك$hk$, $hk$what's new? / how are things?$hk$, $hk$aysh akhbaarak$hk$, $hk$Greeting$hk$, $hk$The second question after كيف حالك, and the one that shows you know Yemeni: ايش is the Yemeni 'what', never the Gulf شخبارك. The reply is the same بخير الحمد لله or a simple تمام.$hk$, $hk$Two friends sitting on a low wall with tea glasses, one asking with raised eyebrows.$hk$, $hk$ايش أخبارك يا محمد؟$hk$, $hk$aysh akhbaarak ya muḥammad?$hk$, $hk$What's new, Mohammed?$hk$, 13)
