  ($hk$حليب$hk$, $hk$milk$hk$, $hk$ḥaliib$hk$, $hk$Drink$hk$, $hk$Fresh milk is حليب; لبن in Yemen is buttermilk — the sour drink served with saltah — so do not use it for milk. شاهي حليب is the milky tea of the south.$hk$, $hk$A glass of white milk beside a small jug on a wooden table.$hk$, $hk$شاهي حليب لو سمحت$hk$, $hk$shaahi ḥaliib law samaḥt$hk$, $hk$Milk tea, please$hk$, 5),
