  ($hk$دكان$hk$, $hk$shop$hk$, $hk$dukkaan$hk$, $hk$Place$hk$, $hk$The corner shop; plural دكاكين. محل is a bigger or newer shop, بقالة a grocery. Doubled ك and long aa.$hk$, $hk$A small open-fronted shop stacked with tins, biscuits and water bottles, the owner at the counter.$hk$, $hk$الدكان قدّام الجامع$hk$, $hk$id-dukkaan guddaam ij-jaamiʿ$hk$, $hk$The shop is in front of the mosque$hk$, 9),
